// ═══ ArrayBlockingQueue — fixed size, ONE lock ═══
BlockingQueue<String> abq = new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(100);
// Fixed capacity: 100. Array-backed. ONE ReentrantLock for ALL operations.
// put() and take() CANNOT run concurrently (same lock)!
// Fair mode: new ArrayBlockingQueue<>(100, true) → FIFO for waiting threads.
// Use: bounded buffer when fairness needed.

// ═══ LinkedBlockingQueue — TWO locks! ═══
BlockingQueue<String> lbq = new LinkedBlockingQueue<>(1000);
// Linked nodes. TWO separate locks: putLock + takeLock!
// put() and take() CAN run concurrently → higher throughput!
// Bounded (capacity specified) or unbounded (no capacity → dangerous!).
// Use: producer-consumer with high throughput. ThreadPoolExecutor default.

// ═══ PriorityBlockingQueue — heap-ordered, unbounded ═══
BlockingQueue<Trade> pbq = new PriorityBlockingQueue<>(100,
    Comparator.comparing(Trade::getPriority).reversed());  // highest first!
// Min-heap internally. poll() returns SMALLEST (or highest priority via Comparator).
// UNBOUNDED — never blocks on put()! Only blocks on take() when empty.
// NOT FIFO! Order by priority, not insertion order!
// Use: priority task processing (high-value trades first).

// ═══ SynchronousQueue — ZERO capacity, direct handoff! ═══
BlockingQueue<String> sq = new SynchronousQueue<>();
// NO internal storage! put() blocks until take(), take() blocks until put()!
// Direct handoff: producer → consumer, no buffering.
// Used by: Executors.newCachedThreadPool() → creates thread per task if none idle!
// Use: when you want immediate handoff with no queuing.

// ═══ DelayQueue — elements released after delay ═══
DelayQueue<DelayedTask> dq = new DelayQueue<>();
dq.put(new DelayedTask("task1", 5, TimeUnit.SECONDS));
// take() blocks until the element's delay expires!
// Elements must implement Delayed interface (getDelay() method).
// Use: scheduled execution, retry with backoff, cache expiration.

// ═══ COMPARISON ═══
// Queue              Capacity    Locks   Order     Blocking   Use Case
// ArrayBlockingQueue  fixed       1       FIFO      put+take   bounded, fair
// LinkedBlockingQueue bounded/unb 2       FIFO      put+take   producer-consumer
// PriorityBlockingQ   unbounded   1       priority  take only  priority processing
// SynchronousQueue    0           N/A     handoff   put+take   direct handoff
// DelayQueue          unbounded   1       delay     take only  scheduled tasks
